stateDiagram-v2
  PLAYING --> END_REQUESTED: captain or game delegate requests end (score deadline starts)
  END_REQUESTED --> PLAYING: requester cancels
  END_REQUESTED --> PLAYING: opponent rejects
  END_REQUESTED --> END_REQUESTED: requester submits own scores
  END_REQUESTED --> AWAITING_SCORE: opponent submits scores and confirms end
  AWAITING_SCORE --> VALIDATING_RESULT: both teams submit
  AWAITING_SCORE --> AWAITING_SCORE: first team submitted (persist and wait)
  VALIDATING_RESULT --> INVALID_SCORE: validation fails
  INVALID_SCORE --> AWAITING_SCORE: submissions reset, first team resubmits
  VALIDATING_RESULT --> COMPLETED: valid final score
  END_REQUESTED --> CANCELLED: score deadline passed (default 5 min)
  AWAITING_SCORE --> CANCELLED: score deadline passed
  INVALID_SCORE --> CANCELLED: score deadline passed
  AWAITING_SCORE --> COMPLETED: admin decides final score
  INVALID_SCORE --> COMPLETED: admin decides final score
  PLAYING --> CANCELLED: admin cancels
  CANCELLED --> LEFT_QUEUE: both teams leave queue, no player history
  COMPLETED --> CHECK_IN_CLOSED: close game check-in session
  COMPLETED --> ACTIVE_QUERY_CLEARED: active court query no longer returns gameId
  COMPLETED --> RECENT_RESULTS: query completed games by unique gameId
  COMPLETED --> DECIDING_CONTINUE: first consecutive win
  DECIDING_CONTINUE --> HOLDING_COURT: winner chooses to continue
  DECIDING_CONTINUE --> LEFT_QUEUE: winner chooses not to continue or 180-second deadline passes
  HOLDING_COURT --> PLAYING: first ready challenger (no new check-in, roster locked)
  COMPLETED --> RESTING: second consecutive win
  COMPLETED --> DECIDING_REQUEUE: losing team (180 seconds)
  DECIDING_REQUEUE --> WAITING: captain chooses requeue
  DECIDING_REQUEUE --> LEFT_QUEUE: leave or PostgreSQL deadline timeout
  RESTING --> WAITING: rest game on same court ends, returns at queue head
